Atlas assets — licence
======================

This directory holds atlas GEOMETRY, TEXTURES and LABEL SETS. It is licensed
separately from the code in this repository, which is Apache-2.0 (see the
LICENSE at the repository root).

The separation is structural, not cosmetic. Assets here arrive under a
share-alike licence, and that obligation must be able to reach the assets and
the assets alone. `tools/check-licence-separation.mjs` enforces the boundary on
every push: no code package may depend on or import this package, and no
asset bytes may be embedded in the shipped JavaScript bundle. Assets are
served as separate files, each carrying its own licence and attribution.

Licence of the assets themselves: SETTLED — D1, 2026-10-09
----------------------------------------------------------

Decision D1 on DOG-2, approved by the repository owner on 2026-10-09: the body
geometry comes from BodyParts3D under CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan. The consequences,
which this file is where they land:

  * Attribution to DBCLS ships with the assets. The required string is
    reproduced verbatim in `attribution.json` and rendered into
    `ATTRIBUTION.md` and into the built site.

  * Everything in this package that derives from those meshes is SHARE-ALIKE.
    Derived files are licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 International, which is the current
    version of the same licence with the same elements.

  * **The atlas geometry therefore cannot be made proprietary.** That is a
    consequence of D1, not of this file, and reversing it is the owner's
    decision and not an engineering one.

  * Code packages remain Apache-2.0 and take no build-time dependency on any
    asset licence. First-party assets in this package stay Apache-2.0 and are
    listed as such; share-alike applies per asset, not per directory.

`docs/asset-licensing.md` is the memo: what was measured upstream, including a
discrepancy in how DBCLS states the licence that the owner should know about,
and the separate and still-unresolved question of the brain parcellation
licence.

Per-asset licensing is declared in `attribution.json` and rendered into the
build as `ATTRIBUTION.md`; `attribution.json` is the authority and every entry
in it must name a licence, a holder and a source. CI fails if any payload file
in this package is not covered by exactly one such entry.
